# Code style guidelines
- Event handler methods which just do one action that could also be done directly in the template are okay to keep.
- Names that signal intent are more desirable than short names.
- Comment line should not exceed 80 chars.
- Comment lines should never have less than 2 words.
- Exports and object properties should be ordered in alphabetical order.
- Callback parameters must not shadow outer-scope bindings.
- Test factory functions that interact with stores must call
  `assertActivePinia` before accessing any store.
- Prefer store-backed factory helpers (`addNew*ToStore`) for test setup
  over calling store actions directly, except when the store action itself
  is the subject under test.
